invariant: INV-55
file: src/tcp_seal.c
catches: tcp_nonblocking_loop_test
reason: ch_seal_in_place seals under the current key whatever
  records_before_key_update answers, so a peer's request for an answer
  never gets one, which RFC 9846 §4.7.3 owes before the next record of
  application data, and an AES-GCM key seals past its ceiling. The loop's
  owed KeyUpdate case requires the record in side.

--- old
    if (records_before_key_update(t) >= count) {
--- new
    if (1) {
